**Version**: 1.2 — 2026-08-13. v1.1 added the core-plus-two-axes family structure and the CAPABILITIES-ARE-SCOPED invariant. v1.2 carries David's ratify of [DD-PRIMER-HOME-CORPUS]: option A, ONE home corpus for every family, in the versioned composeio repo — with option B EXCLUDED BY A GOVERNANCE CONSTRAINT rather than outweighed, because deployment data corpora must not be checked into github and a family that cannot be linted in one pass cannot be warranted. Added [CXC-PRIMER-DEPLOYMENT-CORPORA] for David's "ZB will have several corpora": a domain family names the LIVE REGISTRY and a `domain_suffix` filter, never an inventory. Everything else in v1.1 stands — the axes, the two-sided `authority` assertion, the derived-family-names test, the core-query-as-guard, and the per-instance token ceiling.
**Status**: Draft — awaiting the architect's ratify. Each family's own document is the follow-on deliverable ([CXC-PRIMER-NOT-AUTHORED-HERE]).
